Feature: HTTP security acceptance tests of the deployed API (DevSecOps Phase 2 - Acceptance)

  Background:
    Given "curl" is installed
    And the following profile:
      | name     | value                      |
      | base_url | http://192.168.56.10:8089  |

  Scenario: The application is up and healthy
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s <base_url>/student/actuator/health
      """
    Then the output should contain "UP"

  Scenario: The environment actuator endpoint (config and secrets) is not exposed
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s -o /dev/null -w "code=%{http_code}" <base_url>/student/actuator/env
      """
    Then the output should contain "code=404"

  Scenario: The heap dump actuator endpoint (memory contents) is not exposed
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s -o /dev/null -w "code=%{http_code}" <base_url>/student/actuator/heapdump
      """
    Then the output should contain "code=404"

  Scenario: HTTP TRACE is disabled (Cross-Site Tracing)
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s -o /dev/null -w "code=%{http_code}" -X TRACE <base_url>/student/students/getAllStudents
      """
    Then the output should not contain "code=200"

  Scenario: HTTP security headers are present (clickjacking, MIME sniffing, CSP)
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s -D - -o /dev/null <base_url>/student/actuator/health
      """
    Then the output should contain "X-Frame-Options: DENY"
    And the output should contain "X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff"
    And the output should contain "Content-Security-Policy:"

  Scenario: Invalid input does not leak a Java stack trace
    When I launch a "curl" attack with:
      """
      curl -s <base_url>/student/students/getStudent/not-a-number
      """
    Then the output should not contain "Exception"
    And the output should not contain "at org.springframework"
